course: dictionary
lesson: 1917
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word comeback has three meanings, and the words around it show you which one. Think of a team that is losing badly and then wins. «The team made a great comeback» means they became successful again after a bad time.
explain: In the playground, a comeback can be a quick, clever reply to an insult or a joke. «The coolest comebacks aim at the reason» means the best replies answer the real point. Some pupils think a clever reply must be mean, but a calm, kind reply can be even better.
explain: Look at the form of the word too. «Come back» written as two words is a verb, and it means to return: «Come back soon!» If the word has «a» or «comebacks» in front of it, it is a noun, and it means a comeback.
fact: Comeback can be a noun, meaning a return to success or popularity, or a quick clever reply.
fact: «Make a comeback» and «stage a comeback» both mean to become successful or popular again.
fact: «A quick comeback» is a clever answer to an insult or a joke.
fact: In music and fashion, an old style or an old star can make a comeback.
fact: «Come back» as two words is a verb, and it means to return.
exercise: «The team was losing badly, but they made a great comeback and won.» What does comeback mean here? | A quick, clever reply to a joke | Ran away from the game | *Became successful again after a bad time | A bag for kit
exercise: «Come back soon!» What does come back mean? | To be very angry | To shout loudly | *To return | To go on a trip far away
exercise: «Ben's reply was a quick comeback that made everyone laugh.» What is a quick comeback? | A new pair of trainers | A loud noise | *A clever answer to an insult or a joke | A slow, tired walk
test: «Rachel Carson's book helped the bald eagle make a comeback.» What does make a comeback mean? | *Become successful again after a bad time | Build a nest | Lose all its feathers | Fly away for ever
test: Which reply is a kind, calm comeback to a mean joke? | Hit back as hard as you can | *Stay calm and answer without hurting anyone | Shout at the joker until they cry | Pretend you cannot hear
exam: «The singer's old style is set to make a comeback.» What does this tell you? | Lost for ever | Sold out of tickets | *Popular again | Moved to a new town
